  (text "Note: Do not try to run this amolifier with an actual speaker\nunless you're willing to sacrifice some cheap transistors.\nIt is pushing the small signal-transistors right to their limit with\na purely resistive load, and is likely to fail with a reactive load."
    (at 200.66 182.88 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 3eaf2f34-a245-49f2-bf9e-630d1f8d4ce5)
  )
  (text "C101, C102: Aluminum electrolytic, 15V or higher.\nC103-C111: Ceramic, X7R or Y5V, 15V or higher.\nR101-R109, R111: 1.4 W, 1% metal film.\nR110: 10R, 5 W ceramic-encased wirewound.\nRV101: 10k multiturn trimpot."
    (at 215.9 168.91 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 64edd57c-2bea-4522-912d-ae4ea939d755)
  )
  (text "Rev. B: [B5] Change R109/R109 to 1R3 from 1R2 because no 1R2 were on hand.\n        [A2] Change test procedure to reflect different R109/R109 values.\n        [C2] Add R111 to the input to ensure correct operation when AWG\n             is disconnected.\nRev. C: [A1/A2] Change quiescent current in demo procedure to 25 mA\n                (and quiescent voltage to 65 mV) to match video narration."
    (at 15.24 166.37 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 67d39f74-f6f6-4d6d-872f-5b27209f974f)
  )
  (text "Driver\nstage" (at 182.88 144.78 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 73cc934d-d4e4-4f11-9b73-7467d8404ff8)
  )
  (text "Dummy\nload" (at 243.84 144.78 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 746be51a-5389-456b-80cf-3a7d640e855a)
  )
  (text "AWG" (at 15.24 113.03 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 7830eff2-c83f-4ac0-97c5-4a3b0914a3b5)
  )
  (text "Power entry\nand bypassing" (at 46.99 101.6 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 7b0170b2-7c37-4b44-858c-a50154068b57)
  )
  (text "Unused\nop amp" (at 53.34 147.32 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 9cf9939e-0a19-4999-95ee-b92b9306fbb3)
  )
  (text "Quiescent\ncurrent\nregulation" (at 143.51 148.59 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid c9b36e4e-7f9b-457d-a805-343ce41d3d47)
  )
  (text "Output\nstage" (at 210.82 144.78 0)
    (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid d4d3015b-0e54-4a65-a780-76f76715ceaa)
  )
  (text "Procedure:\n\nAdjust RV101 fully counter-clockwise.  Apply ±6 V to J102.\nDo not connect AWG.\n\nWith millivoltmeter monitoring TP101-TP102, adjust for 65 mV. \n(25 mA quiescent current.)\n\nConnect AWG to J101 and oscilloscope to TP103.\n\nSet AWG for 500 mV, 1kHz sine wave. Observe crossover distortion\n(or lack thereof).\n\nIncrease AWG output level while observing on oscilloscope and\nthermal camera. Quit when there is evidence of circuit clipping\nor of overheating.\n\nTry various frequencies from 20 Hz to 20 kHz - observe whether\ncircuit is fast enough.\n"
    (at 16.51 55.88 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid d5b57d25-f587-4fe0-beeb-bba3641bc721)
  )
  (text "POWER\nSUPPLY" (at 13.97 83.82 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid d8f389b0-07cd-4b9a-94ce-b533531bba37)
  )
  (text "Input buffer and\nfeedback control" (at 100.33 144.78 0)
    (effects (font (face "KiCad Font") (size 2.54 2.54)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid fc10b219-116a-4ba1-9fb9-6e54e3dc2c15)
  )

